<title>BELGIUM: EU agrees monthly malt export refund review.</title>
<headline>EU agrees monthly malt export refund review.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Euroipean Union's cereals management committee on Thursday agreed to revert to a monthly review system for malt export refunds, an EU offiical said.</p>
<p>&quot;The committee fixed the annual refunds at 32.5 Ecus per tonne for barley malt, 38 ecus per tonne for roasted malt and zero for wheat malt,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The Commission is reverting to the old system of two years ago and licences will be awarded on a one month plus 11 basis (August to September).</p>
<p>&quot;This means that the export refund can once again be reviewed on a month by month basis which is what European maltsters were asking for,&quot; the official said.</p>
</text>
